**5. [M]** Count the interleavings, modulo $10^9 + 7$. (`aabcc`, `dbbca`, `aadbbcbcac` $\to$ 3; `aa`, `aa`, `aaaa` $\to$ 6.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
The boolean table with OR replaced by addition. A letter offered by both strings can be attributed either way, and those are different colourings.

::: {#f97fe6d1 .cell execution_count=95}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def count_inter(a, b, c):
    if len(a) + len(b) != len(c):
        return 0
    dp = [[0] * (len(b) + 1) for _ in range(len(a) + 1)]
    dp[0][0] = 1
    for i in range(len(a) + 1):
        for j in range(len(b) + 1):
            if i and a[i - 1] == c[i + j - 1]:
                dp[i][j] = (dp[i][j] + dp[i - 1][j]) % MOD
            if j and b[j - 1] == c[i + j - 1]:
                dp[i][j] = (dp[i][j] + dp[i][j - 1]) % MOD
    return dp[-1][-1]

assert count_inter("aabcc", "dbbca", "aadbbcbcac") == 3
assert count_inter("aa", "aa", "aaaa") == 6
```
:::


