**6. [E]** [LC 392 · Is Subsequence](https://leetcode.com/problems/is-subsequence/){difficulty="Easy"}. (`abc` in `ahbgdc` is true; `axc` in `ahbgdc` is false.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
One pointer walks the pattern and advances only on a match. Existence is this scan. The count is the grid of pattern 3.

::: {#ba3e58df .cell execution_count=96}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def is_subseq(s, t):
    i = 0
    for ch in t:
        if i < len(s) and s[i] == ch:
            i += 1
    return i == len(s)

assert is_subseq("abc", "ahbgdc") is True
assert is_subseq("axc", "ahbgdc") is False
```
