**9. [H]** [LC 87 · Scramble String](https://leetcode.com/problems/scramble-string/){difficulty="Hard"}. (`great` / `rgeat` is true; `abcde` / `caebd` is false; `a` / `a` is true.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
A cut splits both strings. The right part is either in order or swapped. Equal multisets are necessary; without that prune the recursion repeats itself.

::: {#c0ed8a5e .cell execution_count=99}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def is_scramble(a, b):
    memo = {}

    def f(a, b):
        if (a, b) in memo:
            return memo[a, b]
        if a == b:
            memo[a, b] = True
            return True
        if sorted(a) != sorted(b):
            memo[a, b] = False
            return False
        ok = False
        for i in range(1, len(a)):
            if f(a[:i], b[:i]) and f(a[i:], b[i:]):
                ok = True
                break
            if f(a[:i], b[-i:]) and f(a[i:], b[:-i]):
                ok = True
                break
        memo[a, b] = ok
        return ok

    return f(a, b)

assert is_scramble("great", "rgeat") is True
assert is_scramble("abcde", "caebd") is False
assert is_scramble("a", "a") is True
```
:::


