**10. [M]** Optimal string alignment: insert, delete, replace, and one adjacent swap, with no letter in two operations. (`ca` / `ac` $\to$ 1; `abcdef` / `badcfe` $\to$ 3; `ca` / `abc` $\to$ 3.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
The edit table, plus $dp[i - 2][j - 2] + 1$ when the last two letters are a transposition.

::: {#9fbd2dd4 .cell execution_count=100}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def osa(a, b):
    n, m = len(a), len(b)
    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i in range(n + 1):
        dp[i][0] = i
    for j in range(m + 1):
        dp[0][j] = j
    for i in range(1, n + 1):
        for j in range(1, m + 1):
            cost = 0 if a[i - 1] == b[j - 1] else 1
            dp[i][j] = min(dp[i - 1][j] + 1, dp[i][j - 1] + 1, dp[i - 1][j - 1] + cost)
            if i > 1 and j > 1 and a[i - 1] == b[j - 2] and a[i - 2] == b[j - 1]:
                dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][j], dp[i - 2][j - 2] + 1)
    return dp[n][m]

assert osa("ca", "ac") == 1
assert osa("abcdef", "badcfe") == 3
assert osa("ca", "abc") == 3
```
:::


