**11. [M]** `x+` means one or more copies of `x`. (`aab` / `a+b` is true; `b` / `a+b` is false; `abbbc` / `ab+c*` is true; empty / `a+` is false.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
`x+` is `xx*`. Expand the pattern and run the regex table.

::: {#1eeb4473 .cell execution_count=101}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def expand_plus(p):
    out, i = [], 0
    while i < len(p):
        if i + 1 < len(p) and p[i + 1] == "+":
            out.extend([p[i], p[i], "*"])
            i += 2
        else:
            out.append(p[i])
            i += 1
    return "".join(out)

def regex_plus(s, p):
    return regex_tab(s, expand_plus(p))

assert regex_plus("aab", "a+b") is True
assert regex_plus("b", "a+b") is False
assert regex_plus("abbbc", "ab+c*") is True
assert regex_plus("", "a+") is False
```
:::


