**13. [M]** [AC abc130_e · Common Subsequence](https://atcoder.jp/contests/abc130/tasks/abc130_e). Pairs of equal subsequences, empty included. ($(1, 3)$ and $(3, 1) \to 3$.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
Skip either side, and subtract the double-counted skip of both. A match also adds the pairs that end with this common value.

::: {#b75f954c .cell execution_count=103}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def common_pairs(s, t):
    n, m = len(s), len(t)
    dp = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]
    for i in range(n + 1):
        dp[i][0] = 1
    for j in range(m + 1):
        dp[0][j] = 1
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(m):
            dp[i + 1][j + 1] = (dp[i + 1][j] + dp[i][j + 1] - dp[i][j]) % MOD
            if s[i] == t[j]:
                dp[i + 1][j + 1] = (dp[i + 1][j + 1] + dp[i][j]) % MOD
    return dp[n][m]

assert common_pairs([1, 3], [3, 1]) == 3
```
:::


