**14. [M]** Strings of length $n$ over `a..z` that do not contain the word `p`, modulo $10^9 + 7$. ($n = 3$, `ab` $\to$ 17524; $n = 5$, `aba` $\to$ 11879349.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
The avoid automaton with both bounds free. $26^3 - 2 \cdot 26 = 17524$, since `ab` fits in two windows of a length-3 string and those windows cannot both match.

::: {#6cfed40a .cell execution_count=104}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def avoid_word(n, p):
    go = _evil_go(p)
    m = len(p)
    dp = [0] * (m + 1)
    dp[0] = 1
    for _ in range(n):
        nxt = [0] * (m + 1)
        for k in range(m):
            if not dp[k]:
                continue
            for c in range(26):
                nk = go[k][c]
                if nk < m:
                    nxt[nk] = (nxt[nk] + dp[k]) % MOD
        dp = nxt
    return sum(dp) % MOD

assert avoid_word(3, "ab") == 17524
assert avoid_word(5, "aba") == 11879349
```
:::


