**16. [M]** [LC 2486 · Append Characters to String to Make Subsequence](https://leetcode.com/problems/append-characters-to-string-to-make-subsequence/){difficulty="Medium"}. (`coaching`, `coding` $\to$ 4; `abcde`, `a` $\to$ 0; `z`, `abcde` $\to$ 5.)

::: {.callout-note collapse="true" title="Solution"}
Greedily match the longest prefix of `t` as a subsequence of `s`. The unmatched suffix of `t` has to be appended.

::: {#6442edb3 .cell execution_count=106}
``` {.python .cell-code}
def append_chars(s, t):
    j = 0
    for ch in s:
        if j < len(t) and ch == t[j]:
            j += 1
    return len(t) - j

assert append_chars("coaching", "coding") == 4
assert append_chars("abcde", "a") == 0
assert append_chars("z", "abcde") == 5
```
:::


